---

# Final Principle

The Bulgarian Split Squat develops strength where combat athletes most often express it:

one leg at a time,

under unstable conditions,

while maintaining force,

balance,

and postural control.

For this reason, it is one of the highest-value unilateral exercises in the CAS knowledge base.